# REQUIRES: cvc5
# cvc5 computes closed applications, checks counterexamples, and proves the
# bounded and inductive goals by induction on their exact arithmetic, but it
# does not settle the nonlinear lemma, its machine-arithmetic use, or the
# accumulator, so those stay unresolved there, as do the functions relying on
# that lemma; Z3 is the backend for recursive specs.
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --backend=cvc5 %S/spec_automation.cpp -- 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s

# CHECK-DAG: Verified: computed [backend=cvc5]
# CHECK-DAG: verification failed: computed_wrong {{.*}}[backend=cvc5]
# CHECK-DAG: Verified: bounded [backend=cvc5]
# CHECK-DAG: verification failed: bounded_wrong {{.*}}[backend=cvc5] [reason=counterexample]
# CHECK-DAG: Verified: inductive [backend=cvc5]
# CHECK-DAG: Unresolved: accumulated [backend=cvc5] [reason=spec.fuel] {{.*}}induction following accumulate and induction following sum and induction on n did not prove it; if the claim holds, it needs a proof by induction
# CHECK-DAG: Verified: accumulate_sum [backend=cvc5]
# CHECK-DAG: Verified: accumulated_by_lemma [backend=cvc5]
# CHECK-DAG: Unresolved: sum_closed [backend=cvc5]
# CHECK-DAG: Unresolved: gauss [backend=cvc5] [reason=solver.unknown]
# CHECK-DAG: Unresolved: steps [backend=cvc5] [reason=callee.contract] (relies on the contract of sum_closed, which is not established)
